## Required audit procedure

1. Read the complete `ideation/hypothesis_brief.yaml`,
   `ideation/selected/selected_candidate.json`,
   `ideation/selected/t45_search_targets.json`, `literature/synthesis.md` and
   `literature/comparison_table.csv` when present.  Enumerate note directories before opening concrete relevant cards; never pass a directory to
   `read_file`.
2. For every draft hypothesis, call `extract_mechanism_tuple` and
   `extract_design_rationale_tuple`.  Use the compact researcher-facing H1, H2... ID as `source_id`; the runtime needs one tuple file per hypothesis.
3. Compare local evidence first.  Use no more than one focused external query per mechanism cluster, plus one narrower clarification only when the first query succeeds and a material ambiguity remains.  On a retrieval failure, 停止本轮全部同义、近似和改写的外部查询；do not mutate the query and retry.
4. Distinguish a confirmed true collision from a mechanism collision, explanatory competition, a required baseline, and an unverified gap.
   Determine both collision axis and ambition axis.  A routine contribution must not receive an unconditional pass.
5. Write `ideation/novelty_audit.md` and, if any real high/medium-overlap case exists, write `ideation/collision_cases.md`.

## Workspace write contract

- For a new audit or a full Markdown replacement, call
  `write_file(path="ideation/novelty_audit.md", content="...")`.
- For one precise update to an existing text, call
  `edit_file(path="...", old_text="unique existing text", new_text="replacement")`.
  `old_string` / `new_string` are equivalent compatibility field names. Never call `edit_file` with empty arguments.
- This phase writes only Markdown audit files and tuple tools' own JSON. Do not use either file tool for formalization YAML/JSON artifacts; those belong to the next phase and require `write_structured_file`.

## Required audit report structure

Use this Markdown structure.  The report is the proper home for Level labels, collision labels, candidate lineage and required baselines; they must not leak into later researcher-facing Proposal prose.

```markdown
# Novelty Audit

## H1: <short title>
### Hypothesis summary
### Local evidence and search strategy
Evidence used: `<exact literature/... note path or citation key>` → <how it changed the collision, baseline, or boundary judgment>. Repeat only for sources that affected the decision. If none did, write `Evidence used: none` and explain the conditional boundary.
### Similar work and collision assessment
### Collision Axis
### Ambition Axis
### Contribution Distance
### Required baselines and must-not-claim boundary
### Novelty level

## H2: ...

## Final Gate Verdict
Final Gate Verdict: pass_to_experiment | pass_with_required_baselines |
return_to_t4 | drop_due_to_collision

## External coverage and evidence boundary
```

Each hypothesis needs a clear Level 0–3 assessment and its own Collision Axis, Ambition Axis and Contribution Distance.  When the verdict is a pass, explain the baseline and claim constraints that the next formalization phase must honor.  Then call `finish_task`.  Stop: do not formalize the project in this context.
